<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ⚠ REPLACED 2026-08-20, NOT AN IN-PLACE TYPE CHANGE. This field was originally deployed as
        a plain Text field (length 20) earlier in this workstream. Salesforce does not support
        converting an existing custom field's type between Text and Text (Encrypted) in place -
        this is a long-standing, stable platform restriction (the Setup UI never offers "Text
        (Encrypted)" as a target when editing an existing Text field, and the same restriction
        applies via the Metadata API). No live `salesforce-api-context`/Tooling API check or web
        search was available in this session to re-confirm this specific fact against this org, so
        this is applied on established platform knowledge, not a live measurement - flagging that
        distinction explicitly, same as every other platform-restriction note in this workstream.

        PATH TAKEN: delete-and-recreate under the SAME field name (Tax_ID__c), not a renamed field
        (e.g. Tax_ID_Encrypted__c). This keeps every existing reference (layouts/Account-Investing
        Entity Layout.layout-meta.xml, both DPEG_IR_* permission sets' fieldPermissions) valid
        without any further edits - only this one file needed to change for the field itself.

        🔴 DEPLOY SEQUENCING (RESOLVED 2026-08-20 - FIELD IS NOW LIVE). This field's mere
        presence in the repo never deletes the old org field by itself (a standard
        `sf project deploy start` is additive; deleting the file from source control is not the
        same as an org-side delete) - the OLD Text Tax_ID__c had to be explicitly deleted from the
        org before the new EncryptedText version could be created, since the two cannot coexist
        under one API name. This field was also still referenced on
        flexipages/Investing_Entity_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml, which blocked the delete until
        those two field items were temporarily stripped from that page - both have since been
        re-added there, unchanged.

        ⚠ UPDATE 2026-08-20 (devops finding, confirmed): an earlier version of this comment
        predicted a 15-day Recycle Bin API-name reservation requiring a manual permanent-erase step
        between delete and recreate. That concern turned out not to apply at all, not merely to be
        avoidable - devops's atomic delete+recreate PACKAGE (both operations in one deploy unit)
        means the API name was never actually released or reserved in the first place, so there was
        no reservation window to work around. This atomic-package approach is the PROVEN, WORKING
        PATTERN for this exact Text -> EncryptedText scenario on this org - Account.Tax_ID__c is
        now live as Encrypted Text (verified, new field Id, correct mask/length) - and should be
        the default approach for any future Text <-> EncryptedText conversion in this project,
        rather than a separate delete-deploy-then-wait-then-create sequence.

        LENGTH CORRECTED 255 -> 175. The requested length was 255, but Encrypted Text custom fields
        have a PLATFORM-ENFORCED MAXIMUM of 175 characters (unrelated to the general 255 cap on
        plain Text fields) - deploying 255 here would fail validation outright. 175 is used instead;
        flagging this deviation from the literal request since it is a hard platform ceiling, not a
        judgment call.

        maskType=lastFour ("Mask Type should be Last Four Characters Clear" per the request) and
        maskChar=asterisk ("Mask Type should be '*'" per the request, which is actually the
        maskChar/mask-CHARACTER property, not a second maskType - EncryptedFieldMaskType and
        EncryptedFieldMaskChar are two separate CustomField attributes) are both valid values from
        Salesforce's documented EncryptedFieldMaskType / EncryptedFieldMaskChar picklists.

        Encrypted Text fields cannot be marked unique or externalId (platform restriction) - this
        field was never externalId/unique, so no further change was needed there.
    -->
    <fullName>Tax_ID__c</fullName>
    <description>The Tax Identification Number (SSN, EIN, or ITIN) for this investing entity, used for tax reporting (K-1 issuance) and AML/KYC compliance. Stored as Text (Encrypted, Classic Encryption) - masked to the last four characters for users without the View Encrypted Data permission.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Enter the entity's SSN, EIN, or ITIN. Only the last four characters are shown unless you have View Encrypted Data access.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Tax ID</label>
    <length>175</length>
    <maskChar>asterisk</maskChar>
    <maskType>lastFour</maskType>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <type>EncryptedText</type>
</CustomField>
